+## Failed session initialization
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting with the same error, provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model work follows the failed initialization, and cleanup receives the same session even when initialization only partially completed ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+
+`afterSession` is deliberately a cleanup hook for attempted turns, including failed initialization. Its invocation does not imply that initialization completed or that a model ran. No new started flag is added: deployers track acquired resources in their hooks and release only resources actually acquired, allowing for absent or partially initialized state.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
